  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IGAD, Institutional Strengthening Action Programme (ISAP), 2022 - 2025 - IGAD, Institutional Strengthening Action Programme (ISAP)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IGAD, Institutional Strengthening Action Programme (ISAP), 2022 - 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att bidra till att adressera IGAD:s institutionella brister, vilka hindrar IGAD fr&#xe5;n att leverera effektivt p&#xe5; sitt mandat kopplat till pelarna i IGAD:s regionala strategi (2021 - 2025). Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r det strategiska partnerskapet kring ISAP IV:s &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka IGAD:s organisatoriska f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga samt den operationella effektiviteten och bygga upp ett sammanh&#xe4;ngande och st&#xe4;rkt samarbete mellan IGAD och intressenter (medlemsstater, givare, privata sektorn, civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer och andra) f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad transparens och ansvarsskyldighet, s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l som effektiv leverans av tj&#xe4;nster. Genuskvalitet &#xe4;r m&#xe5;linriktat genom detta program, det syftar till att ta itu med befintliga klyftor n&#xe4;r det g&#xe4;ller till&#xe4;mpningen av genusanalys i utformningen av program och inf&#xf6;rlivande av genusk&#xe4;nsliga indikatorer i IGAD:s &#xf6;vervaknings- och utv&#xe4;rderingsramverk. IGAD planerar ocks&#xe5; att g&#xf6;ra en uth&#xe5;llig opinionsbildning och lobbyverksamhet bland medlemsstaterna f&#xf6;r att minska oj&#xe4;mlikhetsklyftan och m&#xf6;ta kvinnors och barns prioriteringar och specifika behov. Fr&#xe4;mjande av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och empowerment f&#xf6;r kvinnor &#xe4;r s&#xe5;ledes ett av de sju tematiska omr&#xe5;den som programmet syftar till att leverera. Det geografiska omr&#xe5;de som t&#xe4;cks &#xe4;r Afrikas Horn (Djibouti, Etiopien, Kenya, Somalia, Sydsudan, Sudan och Uganda).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme aims to contribute to address the key institutional performance gaps still hampering IGAD from delivering its mandate in an effective and efficient manner through the pillars of IGAD&#x2019;s Regional Strategy (2021-2025). The overall objective of the strategic partnership of ISAP IV is to reinforce IGAD&#x2019;s corporate performance and operational efficiency and build a coherent and collaborative engagement between IGAD and stakeholders (Member States, development partners, private sector, civil society organizations and others) for increased transparency and accountability, as well as effective delivery of services. Gender quality is targeted through this programme, it aims to address existing gap in terms of the application of gender analysis in the design of programmes and incorporation of gender sensitive indicators in IGAD&apos;s monitoring and evaluation frameworks. IGAD also plans to make sustained advocacy and lobbying among the Member States to narrow the inequality gap and meet the priorities and specific needs of women and children. Thus, Promoting Gender Equality and Women Empowerment is one of the seven thematic areas the program aims to deliver. The targeted geographical area is the Horn of Africa (Djibouti, Ethiopia, Kenya, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan and Uganda).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of ISAP IV is: To reinforce IGADs corporate performance and
operational efficiency and build a coherent and collaborative engagement between
IGAD and stakeholders for increased transparency and accountability.
The objective of ISAP IV contributes to the attainment of the strategic development
objective of the Corporate Development Services Pillar of the IGAD regional strategyfor 2021-25, which is to contribute to transforming IGAD through enhancing its
institutional capacity to effectively and efficiently deliver its mandate. Phase four of ISAP
comprises two expected outcomes:
(1) Corporate performance and operational efficiency of IGAD (Secretariat and
Specialised Institutions) enhanced, and
(2) Collaborative engagement between IGAD (Secretariat and Specialised Institutions)
and stakeholders (Member states, development partners, private sector, civil society
organizations and others) for effective delivery of services and obligations established.</narrative>
  </description>
